{title: Creator of the Stars of Night}
{artist: Proper Sarum Melody · tr. John Mason Neale}
{key: Eb}
{time: 8/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[Gm]Cre[Cm]ator [Bb]of the stars of night, [Eb]Thy [Cm]peo[Fm]ple's [Bb]ev[Ab]er[Eb]las[Bb]ting [Eb]light,
Je[Ab]su, [Bb]Re[Eb]dee[Ab]mer, [Eb]save [Bb]us [Cm]all, And [Gm]hear [Ab]Thy [Eb]ser[Ab]vants [Eb]when [Bb]they [Gm]call.

Verse 2
[Gm]Thou, [Cm]grieving [Bb]that the ancient curse [Eb]Should [Cm]doom [Fm]to [Bb]death [Ab]a [Eb]u[Bb]ni[Eb]verse,
Hast [Ab]found [Bb]the [Eb]med'[Ab]cine, cine, [Eb]full [Bb]of [Cm]grace, To [Gm]save [Ab]and [Eb]heal [Ab]a [Eb]ru[Bb]ined [Gm]race.

Verse 3
[Gm]Thou [Cm]cam'st the [Bb]Bridegroom of the bride, [Eb]As [Cm]drew [Fm]the [Bb]world [Ab]to [Eb]e[Bb]v'ning [Eb]tide;
Pro[Ab]cee[Bb]ding [Eb]from [Ab]a [Eb]vir[Bb]gin [Cm]shrine, The [Gm]spot[Ab]less [Eb]Vic[Ab]tim [Eb]all [Bb]di[Gm]vine.

Verse 4
[Gm]At [Cm]whose dread [Bb]name, majestic now, [Eb]All [Cm]knees [Fm]must [Bb]bend, [Ab]all [Eb]hearts [Bb]must [Eb]bow;
All [Ab]things [Bb]ce[Eb]les[Ab]tial [Eb]Thee [Bb]shall [Cm]own, And [Gm]things [Ab]ter[Eb]res[Ab]trial, [Eb]Lord [Bb]a[Gm]lone.

Verse 5
[Gm]O [Cm]Thou whose [Bb]coming is with dread [Eb]To [Cm]judge [Fm]and [Bb]doom [Ab]the [Eb]quick [Bb]and [Eb]dead,
Pre[Ab]serve [Bb]us [Eb]while [Ab]we [Eb]dwell [Bb]be[Cm]low, From [Gm]e[Ab]very [Eb]in[Ab]sult [Eb]of [Bb]the [Gm]foe.
